K	DiagTrack	svc	19045	Connected User Experiences and Telemetry	Collects and sends Windows diagnostic and usage data to Microsoft.	Diagnostic data upload stops. Feedback Hub and some troubleshooters report less; Windows keeps working.	Disable, restart, use the PC as usual for a few days; check that Windows Update still runs.	4			telemetry upload, not needed for anything on the PC itself			0	0	published	Microsoft's IoT Enterprise services page (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/iot/iot-enterprise/optimize/services) describes this service (Windows 10/11 IoT Enterprise services page).	published	Microsoft's IoT Enterprise services page (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/iot/iot-enterprise/optimize/services) rates it OK to disable (Windows 10/11 IoT Enterprise) and Microsoft's VDI optimization tool (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/The-Virtual-Desktop-Team/Virtual-Desktop-Optimization-Tool/main/2009/ConfigurationFiles/Services.json) disables it for virtual desktops; no Microsoft source Hadron checked says to keep it. Microsoft's Windows 10 2004 VDI guide (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/remote/remote-desktop-services/rds-vdi-recommendations-2004) lists it as a candidate on disconnected networks.						
